cdot(1),\\frac{2\\pi}{3})=(2,\\frac{2\\pi}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we convert $B$ to Cartesian coordinates. To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\   & =2\\cdot\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}) \\\\   & =2\\cdot(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\   & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\   & =2\\cdot\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}) \\\\   & =2\\cdot(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\   & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ are $(-1,\\sqrt{3}).$" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550127 1080 "(8\\sqrt{3},8\\sqrt{3})" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550127 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550127 1083 #uuid "235af48b-73d5-5181-bbf4-d811e601a21f" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550128 1080 "1" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550128 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550128 1083 #uuid "25037821-3854-562c-994e-f296a336d4d5" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550129 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550165 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550129 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550129 1077 "field-2" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550129 1078 #edb/ref 17592186550165 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550129 1079 #uuid "25429db6-9731-5cad-93b2-3769a934d1b3" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550130 1080 "-1" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550130 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550130 1083 #uuid "305b90e4-d28c-5e61-ba1a-abab0ef30825" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [175921865501