s in the fourth quadrant, we have $\\theta=\\frac{7\\pi}{4}.$\n\nConsequently, the polar coordinates of $B$ are\n\n$$\n(2,\\frac{7\\pi}{4}+(-\\frac{\\pi}{4}))=(2,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we convert $B$ to Cartesian coordinates. To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\   & =2\\cdot\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}) \\\\   & =2\\cdot(0) \\\\   & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\   & =2\\cdot\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}) \\\\   & =2\\cdot(-1) \\\\   & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $B$ are $(0,-2).$" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550140 1080 "(16\\sqrt{3},16\\sqrt{3})" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550140 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550140 1083 #uuid "5cf6ceee-b036-5c1f-921c-657626d22fac" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550141 1080 "-1" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550141 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550141 1083 #uuid "5fb777fb-61ce-52be-bae8-b3c80108daf8" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550142 1080 "(-8,0)" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550142 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550142 1083 #uuid "641d2665-d10f-5535-ab2c-72bc489e588d" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550143 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550141 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550143 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550143 1077 "field-1" 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550143 1078 #edb/ref 17592186550141 13194139535967 17592186045443 true] [17592186550143 1079 